a4/notebooks/*
a4/notebooks

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# a4/runs/ — per-campaign output trees. We want to track the *code* and the
# *Pro-facing artifacts* that ship with each campaign, and ignore everything
# else (heavy regeneratable artifacts + POS dispatch byproducts).
#
# TRACKED (re-included below):
#   - analysis code (*.py, *.sh, requirements.txt) anywhere in the tree
#   - reports / plans (*.md), notebooks (*.ipynb), rendered notebooks (*.html)
#   - plots (*.png, *.svg) — typically under plots*/ subdirs
#   - analysis output tables (*.csv) anywhere in the tree
#   - top-level run summary JSONs (a4/runs/<run>/*.json only — deeper JSONs
#     are POS dispatch config/meta noise and stay ignored)
#
# IGNORED (everything else, including):
#   - dbs/ / raw_dbs/ / dbs_internal/ — SQLite DB stores (e.g. iv_pos_7/dbs/
#     is ~1.3 GB)
#   - __pycache__/                    — Python bytecode caches
#   - *.zip                           — packaged delivery archives
#   - POS dispatch byproducts: *.stdout, *.stderr, *.status, *.file,
#     bootstrap scripts, per-node setup PDFs, per-run config/meta JSONs
#
# Strategy: blanket-ignore the tree, then re-include valuable file types.
# To track a new artifact type from a future campaign, add another
# `!a4/runs/**/<pattern>` line below.
#
# NOTE: gitignore semantics require that we re-include directories first
# (so git traverses them) before we can re-include individual files.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
a4/runs/**
# re-include directories so the file-level re-includes below can match
!a4/runs/**/
# re-include valuable code + reports + plots + analysis output tables
!a4/runs/**/*.py
!a4/runs/**/*.md
!a4/runs/**/*.ipynb
!a4/runs/**/*.html
!a4/runs/**/*.png
!a4/runs/**/*.svg
!a4/runs/**/*.csv
!a4/runs/**/*.sh
!a4/runs/**/*.txt
# top-level run summary JSONs only (one level deep under a4/runs/);
# deeper JSONs (e.g. <run>/<timestamp>/config/*.json) stay ignored
!a4/runs/*/*.json
# heavy / generated subtrees: re-ignore so git doesn't even traverse into them
a4/runs/**/dbs/
a4/runs/**/raw_dbs/
a4/runs/**/dbs_internal/
a4/runs/**/__pycache__/

bundles/
dispatch_manifest.json
collection_report.json

